// I Wanted To Say (Comp: Victor Lewis, Recorded Stan Getz 1982)

Tempo 136
Keysig C

Groove Metronome2-4
  z * 2

// Set up a signal track so I, poor jazz player that I am, can
// figure out (somewhat) where in this song I am. Hitting a
// clave at the start of each 4 bar sequence seems to be enough.
// Note how we set the initial groove to force this to a 4 bar 
// pattern. Without this, the pattern would repeat every 2 bars.
// It also loads in the drum includes.

Groove ModernJazz

Begin Drum-Signal
    Tone Claves
    Volume ffff
    Sequence  D1234  z  z  z
    Sticky On
End

Repeat
Groove ModernJazz
1       Am9
2       Em9
3      C#m9
4     G#m11

Groove ModernJazz1

5    F13sus
6       Cm9
7      Am11
8         /

Groove ModernJazzSus

9     D9sus
10    E9sus
11     C#m9
12    G#m11

Groove ModernJazz1Sus

13   F13sus
14      Cm9
15     Am11
16        /

Groove ModernJazz

17   D13sus
18   D13#11
19   D13sus
20   D13#11

Groove ModernJazzSus

21   F13sus
22   F13#11
23     Em11
24   Eb13#11

Groove ModernJazz1Sus

25      Am9
26      Em9
27     C#m9
28    G#m11

RepeatEnding

Groove ModernJazz

29   F13sus
30      Cm9
31   A13sus
32        /

RepeatEnd

Groove ModernJazz2

33   F13sus
34      Cm9

// On the score this is a 2 bar repeat.
// We expand it out make the decrescs easier

Decresc p 2

35   A13sus
Begin Drum-side
  Volume f
  Sequence D13
End
Drum-Ride Volume f
36        /

Groove ModernJazzEnd
Decresc ppp 2

35   A13sus
36        / z!



